<http://data.silknow.org/object/a0d90c15-d80a-3ab6-aaef-78f08ac9cdc8>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Bag, embroidered linen, ca. 1700, French?, coloured silks in stylized flowers, silver-gilt tassels"@en , "By the end of the 17th century, fashionable bags were round in shape.  The pale ground of the embroidery and pattern of brightly coloured flowers in this example are typical of French bags of this period.  Finishing the drawstrings are very ornate tassels of silver-gilt thread.  \n\nThe lack of a more secure fastening than a drawstring suggests that this purse was intended to hold a keepsake or to wrap a gift of money, rather than everyday monetary use."@en , "A flat, shield-shaped bag of linen, embroidered with a rococo stitch ground of white silk with stylized flowers in coloured silks worked in gobelin and back stitches.  The bag is bound with silver-gilt ribbon and has a silver-gilt drawstring with large silver-gilt tassels.  The green silk lining is a later replacement."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/cf9271f9-9847-3bb2-aa90-9ab54191ee54> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "By the end of the 17th century, fashionable bags were round in shape.  The pale ground of the embroidery and pattern of brightly coloured flowers in this example are typical of French bags of this period.  Finishing the drawstrings are very ornate tassels of silver-gilt thread.  \n\nThe lack of a more secure fastening than a drawstring suggests that this purse was intended to hold a keepsake or to wrap a gift of money, rather than everyday monetary use."@en , "A flat, shield-shaped bag of linen, embroidered with a rococo stitch ground of white silk with stylized flowers in coloured silks worked in gobelin and back stitches.  The bag is bound with silver-gilt ribbon and has a silver-gilt drawstring with large silver-gilt tassels.  The green silk lining is a later replacement."@en , "Bag, embroidered linen, ca. 1700, French?, coloured silks in stylized flowers, silver-gilt tassels"@en ;
        ecrm:P43_has_dimension         <http://data.silknow.org/object/a0d90c15-d80a-3ab6-aaef-78f08ac9cdc8/dimension/1> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/a0d90c15-d80a-3ab6-aaef-78f08ac9cdc8/dimension/2> ;
        dc:identifier                  "T.11-1922" ;
        <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs>
                <https://collections.vam.ac.uk/item/O158758> .

